This is a general howto on how to use some of the added features that I created
for this framework.

Suported Image formats.
8bit bmp
24bit bmp
24bit tga unconpressed.

To load an image simply first create a Image object.
ex.
Image ImageName("name of image");

This will create an image object and load the specified file into memory.

Now you will need set the address of the image.
ex.
ImageName.setAddress(name of ps2 framework, 0 for the very first image\
					    1 for any other one that
					      comes after that.);

The the framework is not a problem. Now the second parameter of the setAddress.
There is a problem with how the ps2 texture memory works. The first image to 
load needs its give 2k addres multiplied by 32 then you are good to go.
Any other image after this inital address does not need to multiply
the starting address by 32. This is just a cheap hack for now.
Because each image is independent of each other they do not know which image
is loaded first of not.

